# This tree is cross-compiled from Linux (WSL or a MiSTer). With
# core.autocrlf=true on Windows, a checkout produces CRLF everywhere, and:
#
#   - GNU make reads `BASE = arm-none-linux-gnueabihf<CR>`, so CC becomes
#     `arm-none-linux-gnueabihf<CR>-gcc` and the build dies with
#     "command not found"
#   - every .sh dies with "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M"
#
# Force LF in the working tree regardless of the user's autocrlf setting.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touch these.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.so     binary
*.rbf    binary
*.sof    binary
releases/** binary
